            <ArticleTitle>Atypical teratoid/rhabdoid tumor arising from the trigeminal nerve in an adult.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>447-449</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 30-year-old male presented with left facial pain and numbness. Initial MRI demonstrated an enhancing mass involving the left trigeminal nerve. Follow-up imaging showed interval growth with erosion of the sphenoid body. Surgical resection was performed and immunohistochemistry staining was consistent with an atypical teratoid/rhabdoid tumor. Awareness of this entity and its imaging features such as diffusion restriction, intratumoral hemorrhage, and bony destruction, can help guide confirmatory diagnostic testing and appropriate therapy.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© The Author(s) 2016.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
